Wind Turbine Blades


Design Perspective
–A good Helicopter rotor airfoil ≠ good Wind Turbine rotor airfoil
–Operates in a very different environment
• Airborne particles get stuck to the blades causing roughness effects (Difficult to clean blades regularly)
• Huge structural and aerodynamic loading (in a 1.5 MW turbine, each blade weigh ~ 5 tons)




Design Philosophy and Criteria
oSpecially-tailored airfoils for wind turbines
oLarge thickness airfoils at the root. Thickness reduced closer to the tip
oCriteria
– Moderate to high thickness ratio t/c
• Rigid rotor: 16%–26% t/c
• Flexible rotor: 11%–21% t/c
• Small wind turbines: 10%-16% t/c
– High lift-to-drag ratio
– Minimal roughness sensitivity
– Weak laminar separation bubbles


